{"findings":[
  {"file":"app/views/embed/best.html.erb","line":6,"severity":"critical","category":"bug","title":"Invalid ERB syntax renders the embed/best template unusable","body":"The tag `<%- end if %>` is not valid Ruby/ERB. ERB compiles the tag body as `end if`, which is a Ruby syntax error. Rendering `EmbedController#best` for an existing topic will raise a SyntaxError or ActionView::Template::Error instead of returning the comments, breaking the embed feature. The tag should be `<%- end %>`."},
  {"file":"app/models/topic_embed.rb","line":13,"severity":"critical","category":"security","title":"Unsanitized embed_url in imported HTML footer allows stored XSS","body":"`embed_url` is interpolated directly into an HTML string using `I18n.t('embed.imported_from', link: \"<a href='#{url}'>#{url}</a>\")`, with no HTML escaping. `url` is ultimately user-influenced (passed from `EmbedController#best` through the retrieve job, with only a prefix check for http/https) and is later stored and rendered with `cook_method` raw_html and `raw post.cooked` in the embed view. A URL such as `http://eviltrout.com/'><script>alert(1)</script>` becomes executable HTML in the post, giving stored XSS for anyone viewing the embedded topic. Escape `url` (e.g. with `ERB::Util.html_escape`) before building the footer."},
  {"file":"app/views/layouts/embed.html.erb","line":11,"severity":"high","category":"security","title":"Unescaped referer is injected into JavaScript targetOrigin","body":"`request.referer` is interpolated directly into a JavaScript string inside a `<script>` block without `j`/`escape_javascript`/HTML escaping. Although `ensure_embeddable` validates only the referer's host, the rest of the URL can contain quotes or `</script>`. A referer such as `http://eviltrout.com/foo'></script><script>alert(document.cookie)</script>` would break out of the script and execute in the Discourse embed page. Escape the referer or derive the target origin from configuration rather than embedding the raw header."},
  {"file":"app/jobs/scheduled/poll_feed.rb","line":35,"severity":"medium","category":"bug","title":"PollFeed assumes every RSS item has a content field","body":"`i.content.scrub` calls `String#scrub` on `i.content` unconditionally. RSS/Atom feeds commonly store the body in `description`/`summary` (or omit it for titles-only items); when `content` is nil, this raises `NoMethodError: undefined method 'scrub' for nil:NilClass`, aborting the entire poll before later items are processed. Use `(i.content || i.description || '')` (or equivalent per feed format) and guard nil."},
  {"file":"app/assets/javascripts/embed.js","line":5,"severity":"low","category":"bug","title":"Missing null check for embed container element","body":"`document.getElementById('discourse-comments')` may return `null` if the embedding page omits the expected `<div id='discourse-comments'></div>`. The code then calls `comments.appendChild(iframe)` on line 12, throwing a TypeError and preventing the resize message listener from being registered. Guard with `if (comments)` or explicitly document the required element."}
]}
